1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Nc3 d6 4. Bg5 c6 5. Qd2 b5 6. f4 Nd7 7. Nf3 b4 8. Nd1 Qb6 9. Ne3 Ngf6 10. Bd3 d5 11. Bxf6 (11. e5 {Grefe-Nunn, GRE Masters B 1973 (0-1, 25 moves - annotated in Secrets of Grandmaster Chess by John Nunn. "The following year, Paul Littlewood found the correct reply."}) 11... Nxf6 12. e5 Ng4 ({Now} 12... Ne4 {is bad because g5 is free for the knight:} 13. Bxe4 dxe4 14. Ng5 {leaves the e4-pawn in trouble (Nunn)}) 13. h3 Nxe3 14. Qxe3 {"With advantage to White" (John Nunn, Secrets of Grandmaster Chess by John Nunn, Batsford 1997, p44)} e6 15. O-O Bf8 16. a3 c5 17. axb4 Qxb4 18. c3 {(moves to here given in 'The Pirc for the Tournament Player' by John Nunn (Batsford 1980))} Qb6 19. Nh2 h5 20. Nf3 c4 21. Bc2 Bd7 22. Rab1 a5 23. Ng5 a4 24. Qg3 Rg8 25. Nh7 Be7 26. Nf6+ Bxf6 27. exf6 Qd6 28. Qg5 Rf8 29. Ra1 Kd8 30. Ra2 Kc7 31. Rfa1 Ra6 32. Qh6 Rfa8 33. Qg7 a3 34. bxa3 Rxa3 35. Rxa3 Rxa3 36. Rb1 Rxc3 37. Qg8 Bc8 38. Ba4 Qa3 39. Qxf7+ Kd8 40. Qe8+ {Source: mimeo of unpublished games scores collected by WA Frost and J Nunn. Contributed by Andy Ansel, 24 October 2024.} 1-0

